## Economics

Two revenue streams, combined in Analytics against lead cost, Retell and Twilio spend: outside buyers pay per qualified transfer (buffer reached, e.g. 120/220 s); our agents earn ~$110 per closed policy via commission, with advances and chargeback risk. Retell at 400 dials/day ~$465–815/month by model; after transfer the AI fee stops but telephony continues. Twilio bills both legs during human conversations. **Leads dominate:** ~2,900 fresh leads/month at ~$10 ≈ $29,000/month, reduced by bad-lead credits. Scraping leads advised against ($500–1,500 per call penalties); legitimate cheaper routes: own Facebook forms (human-only unless wording covers AI), aged/shared leads with consent proof, bulk negotiation.

## Legal framing (Claude is not my lawyer and should keep saying so)

AI-voice calls fall under TCPA artificial/prerecorded voice rules: prior express written consent for cell numbers; consent to a lead generator generally doesn't transfer. Human-dialled calls still need national DNC and calling hours. Calling someone who asked not to be called is heavily litigated ($500–1,500 per call). Recording: all-party states (e.g. CA, FL, IL, PA, WA) require telling everyone; recording without notice can be a crime. Selling requires a licence with Life authority in the customer's state. FCC Reassigned Numbers Database not built. Need documented consent per lead, monthly DNC refresh, and attorney review before a real campaign.

